WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.077
DNA has two strands, but only one

00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:02.704
gets read.

00:00:03.331 --> 00:00:03.970
Which one?

00:00:04.597 --> 00:00:06.001
This is the template strand.

00:00:06.628 --> 00:00:09.217
RNA polymerase reads it and builds RNA

00:00:09.264 --> 00:00:09.821
to match.

00:00:10.448 --> 00:00:11.737
This is the coding strand.

00:00:12.131 --> 00:00:13.037
It just sits there.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.512
It does not get read.

00:00:15.231 --> 00:00:16.810
Like a page printed on both sides,

00:00:16.845 --> 00:00:18.250
but you only read the front.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.317
The template strand gets read, and the

00:00:20.351 --> 00:00:21.559
coding strand does not.

00:00:22.186 --> 00:00:23.300
Where does reading start?

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:24.345
Swipe.
